:yrashk yr:built :ycxx .
:ycxx
    a                  yr:Project, schema:CreativeWork ;
    schema:name        "ycxx" ;
    schema:url         <https://github.com/yrashk/ycxx> ;
    schema:description "An independent, resident C++26 compiler." ;
    schema:abstract    "Preprocessor, front end, constant evaluator, code generator, object writer and linker, all its own. It stays resident, holds the whole program's analysis in memory, and recomputes only what a change can affect." ;
    yr:quote           "How far can we get with this?" ;
    yr:voice           "How far can we get with this?" ;
    yr:role            "director" ;
    yr:status          "pre-0.1" ;
    yr:group           "experimental" ;
    yr:sector          <sector/machines> ;
    ord:inOrdering     <ordering/chart> ;
    ord:rank           190 ;
    yr:start           "2026"^^xsd:gYear ;
    yr:weight          3 ;
    yr:position        0.34 ;
    yr:color           "#b9a8ff" ;
    yr:mono            true ;
    yr:repos           ( <repo/yrashk/ycxx> ) ;
    yr:notes           (
        "In one week, from an old idea to compiling a good subset of C++ (classes, templates, constant evaluation) to signed macOS arm64 and static x86-64 Linux executables, with no external compiler, assembler or linker."
        "Watch mode with an interactive trace for people and agents; ycxx policies for affine and linear type checking; its own benchmarking tool."
        "Built by AI agents directed by the author, like libycxx before it. Open to anyone with spare LLM capacity to point at it."
    ) .

